<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10834"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:vscantu1@msn.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vscantu<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vscantu<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 6:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->NANCYDREW: Descriptions of the crime scenes, in case you didn&#39;t &#34;get it&#34;, were not meant to directly give &#34;comfort&#34; to the victims relatives. Tho&#39; they were an obvious attempt to bring them  nearer to &#34;closure&#34;- by solving the case. Us on-line sleuths were trying to find out who the culprit was by analyzing the evidence. You have to dissect the crime scene in minute detail to do this. Or was this something that escaped your intelligence? <BR> <BR>At this time emotions are running high all around. But coming on this board and blasting those who have put in hundreds of hours honestly trying to bring an end to this case is an unfair cheap shot. Unfortunately for you, it didn&#39;t do much more than give you the satisfaction of sounding sanctimonious.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
