<!--Post: 10837--><!--Time: 1110248211-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10837"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, March 07, 2005 - 6:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My name is Lost and I haven’t posted in 5 hours and 43 m…Dooooh! <BR> <BR>Sorry, I’m at it again. <BR> <BR> <BR>NancyDrew! <BR>Goodness sakes! <BR>What happened to the gracious and demure young woman I knew from “The Ghost Dogs of Moon Lake”? <BR>Apparently the years have not been kind to you. <BR>How’s the new hip working out? Did you have a good B.M. this morning? <BR> <BR>Let’s start here. <BR> <BR>“come to grips with the fact that LE caught Rader NO THANKS TO MESSAGE BOARDS…” <BR> <BR>Nancy, Dennis Rader posted here -- more than once. Risky, no?  <BR> <BR>I believe he developed an obsession with what people were saying about him here and a fear that someone might get too close.  <BR>LE were monitoring boards and chats. I.P.s were subpoenaed. <BR> <BR>Tom will eventually share the details of his interplay with investigators. <BR> <BR>Consider this as a possibility: <BR> <BR>“…posters like Huff and Skov and George confounded and yes – mesmerized Rader. They were talking about him…a lot. He had to pay attention. He had to. <BR> <BR>Fame is a bitch. DTM bought in to his own myth and it led to his downfall. <BR> <BR>He should have been mustering all the clarity he was capable of. Instead, he was forced to obsess about his public. <BR> <BR>While he was raging inside over Steve_huff’s wicked critique of his poetry &#40;or peeking out his front window after Steve nailed his description&#41;, he should have been researching how to fake his own death and disappearance. <BR> <BR>When George originally insisted that Marine Hedge and Dee Davis were BTK victims, Denny scheduled more time and less sleep to make sure he didn’t miss a post. <BR>He should have been studying up on exchange rates for Cruzados…” <BR> <BR>Am I delusional,?... or did Rader make a stupid mistake that led to his arrest. <BR>He was rattled, sleepless and furiously motivated to communicate. <BR>It was a floppy disc not a swab or a hunch or deductive reasoning that did him in. <BR> <BR>As far as the surviving victims are concerned: <BR> <BR>I don’t think I ever read a post &#40;and I’ve read them all&#41; where the author suggested that they were doing any survivor a favor.  <BR>I never came across an insinuation that anything short of the capture of BTK would bring about closure. <BR> <BR>Occasionally, the speculative descriptions of Rader’s heinous rituals, bordered on the gratuitous. I’ll give you that.  <BR> <BR>As much as I shudder to think of a survivor reading an account of the torture and murder of their loved one,  <BR>I know that nothing compares with the horror of the movie that plays in their head. <BR> <BR>NancyD, do you feel the same angst in your gut for the survivors when you watch CSI:Miami, or when another Friday the 13th opens wide? <BR>Certainly, something as simple as channel surfing can be a painful roulette for Charlie Otero or Steve Relford. <BR> <BR>Here’s something to think about. <BR> <BR>Nancy Fox.  <BR> <BR>I did not know her. <BR>I have studied her portrait, wondering what she was like. <BR>I know she worked two jobs and lived on her own. <BR>I heard she had a wonderful sense of humor and that she chose her friends carefully. <BR> <BR>Let’s pretend for a moment that Nancy Fox could speak to us. <BR> <BR>Would she be surprised to lean that total strangers were so committed to finding her killer?... <BR>That a woman in Denmark wasn’t going to rest until she threw a net over this madman? <BR> <BR>Would she cheer us on or see us as fools. <BR>Would she tell us to give it up or... to go for it. <BR> <BR>What do you think Drew? <BR> <BR>There may have been some participants here who were in Catch for an inappropriate reason. <BR>They’re gone now, booted or disinterested. <BR>Some good soldiers have faded away too, since the hunt is essentially over. <BR> <BR>As far as I can see, the ones who remain have good intentions. <BR>They’re sticking around for all the reasons I listed in my previous post. <BR> <BR>You are free to go. <BR> <BR>In fact, why don’t you go watch reruns of ‘Murder She Wrote” with the Hardy Boys. <BR> <BR> <BR>MadDog <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10837-->
