look at the avaible knowlege with their crativity and intuition and thereby see new paths and patterns  that could leed that science in a direction the specialist would NEVER have thought of. <BR>&#40;sorry for the helpless explanation, but I think you people will understand anyway he eh&#41; <BR> <BR>Now Blue Puppy can you draw a line from Øvlisens theorie to why people on a forum  working on a crimec case, COULD have value to the police? <BR> <BR>If not! let me know and I´ll try to explain it to you in spite of my bad english<IMG SRC="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/clipart/happy.gif" ALT=":-&#41;" BORDER=0> <BR> <BR>And by the way I think HIGHLY of the rest of you postes here who realy try and DO make a difference. <BR>If I was a relative or friend of one of the BTK victims, it would mean a LOT to me that other people CARED about what happend to their loved once and that wether their postings/research actually had any impact on the investigation/capture of the murderer or not. But I guess that you Blue Puppy dont understand that kind of  emotions. I feel sorry for you puppy! <BR> <BR>And Lost Dog it was very interesting to read your thoughts on the facination/pressure that BTK/Rader? might have felt by reading posters views and theories about him and how that might have influenced his behaivouer that in turn might have made him make a mistake that led police to be able to catch him... <BR> <BR>hugs to you all from skov<!--/Text--></td></tr>
