<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10973"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 3:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Steve <BR> <BR>I love Denmark, the &#34;duck&#34; thing was just ment sweet and loving, you know the H C Andersen &#34;the ugly duck&#34; right? just thinking of the huge distance and big diffenernce in size between US and DK, thinking that DK was a bit like the ugly duck compared to US he he... <BR>  <BR>Actually Denmark is not my original homeland, I lived here for 39 years, but was born in Sweden from a swedish mother and a nowegian father, grew up in Sweden and one yesr in Norway, one year in spain and then moved to DK when I was 10. My heart is still out there in the deep swedish woods... <BR> <BR>Dag Hammarskjöld was a GREAT sweed, statesman BUT also a superb poet, I actually have his last book. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.lysator.liu.se/nordic/authors/hammarda.html" target=_top>http://www.lysator.liu.se/nordic/authors/hammarda. html</a>  <BR> <BR>I LOVE the &#34;Denmarkians&#34;, i`ll remember that one LOL<!--/Text--></td></tr>
