<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10977"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 08, 2005 - 4:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok Embersage, I know this is OT but you don&#39;t come across someone everyday who refers to the sport of rowing as &#39;crew&#39;.  If I had a nickel for every time I&#39;d tell someone I was on the crew team &#40;blank stare&#41; and then expound and say - you know, rowing - I wouldn&#39;t have to be working today. <BR> <BR>Of course this was many many moons ago and was also dependent on where in the country you were, but your comment took me back in time there for a moment. <BR> <BR>And Lostdog - we gotta be neighbors here in Arnoldland &#40;California to those of you not from the left coast&#41;.  If you can see the coast and I can see the coast then that puts us within at least 800 miles of each other, right? <BR> <BR>Funny how this site has brought so many different and yet at times similar people together.  Way cool.  Someone needs to thank Al Gore for inventing the Internet &#40;lol&#41;! <!--/Text--></td></tr>
