</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 09, 2005 - 8:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->DEAR FRIENDS I RECIEVED THIS IN MY EMAIL TODAY AND BASICALLY HAVE HAD ENOUGH, MAYBE I WAS  A LITTLE OVERPOSTING YET WAS ONLY TRYING TO HELP. i WILL NO LONGER BE POSTING BECAUSE I AM TIRED OF BEING HARASSED FOR TRYING TO HELP. tHANKS E. <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Dear &#34;Embersageblue&#34;: <BR> <BR>I sent an email requesting credentials to post this myself; <BR>however, I believe Tom is vacationing and I will not be <BR>able to post this in time. If you have the chance, please <BR>post the below for me on the CatchBTK.com message board <BR>under &#34;Post-Arrest Obsessed posters&#34;. <BR> <BR>Dear Embersageblue and the &#34;dirty dozen&#34;, <BR> <BR>I too think there are a few folks taking the &#34;Catch BTK&#34; <BR>post arrest a bit too far, especially yourself and your so <BR>called &#34;dirty dozen&#34;. <BR> <BR>I do believe your constant need to post the most minute <BR>detail &#40;which is not in itself a bad thing, but please keep <BR>it to one thread&#41; and interacting with folks as if this <BR>were a variation of Instant Messenger after the BTK release <BR>is the reason certain individuals are becoming upset at <BR>your and others&#39; actions. <BR> <BR>I am both relieved and even more interested in the post BTK <BR>arrest details that will become available; however, there <BR>is a limit to the volume of information and your structure, <BR>for normal individuals can keep up with.  Coming back to <BR>the site and seeing the repeat &#34;Dennis Rader Timeline&#34; on <BR>various threads and constant links to your other postings <BR>has become very tiresome and way too difficult to keep up <BR>with as each version could pose new details. <BR> <BR>There is a constant attack concerning how the Wichita <BR>Police Department &#40;aka &#34;LE&#34; on this board&#41; has handled the <BR>case, and I am very certain the barrage of <BR>unnecessary/invalid information they would have had to <BR>manage from folks like you is the main reason they have <BR>withheld details thus far. <BR> <BR>Thanks for at least teaching me one thing about this case, <BR>and please cut back to relevant information.  If you would <BR>like to interact within folks on a more frequent basis, <BR>please exchange email addresses with other folks and <BR>provide a report of your findings. <BR> <BR>Sincerely, <BR> <BR>Woolpainter <BR> <BR> <BR>         <BR>__________________________________  <BR>Do you Yahoo!?  <BR>Yahoo! Mail - Easier than ever with enhanced search. Learn more.  <BR><a href="http://info.mail.yahoo.com/mail_250" target=_top>http://info.mail.yahoo.com/mail_250</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
