<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11123"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 12:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Damn Victor, I&#39;m trying to be all diplomatic and stuff and you come along and play id to my superego &#40;or something like that&#41; and say exactly what I was really thinking. <BR> <BR>She is intelligent, and somewhat eloquent...but she&#39;s a whackjob, and this show is proving it conclusively, IMNHO. She has nearly all the facts of the BTK case wrong. She stated he began killing at 38 - we know that&#39;s wrong. She keeps referring to him as - I can&#39;t believe this - &#34;the killer in <b>Kansas City</b>&#34; <BR> <BR>Sounds like she&#39;s basically made her reputation being a contrarian of sorts. She was, after all, the psychiatrist who testified that John Gacy, one of your more organized and competent serials, was insane in the legal sense. A load of crap, if you ask me. She probably thinks DTDC is nuts, too, in spite of the very sane way he kept himself hidden and seeming proper all these years. <BR> <BR>She actually sounds drunk, to tell the most blatant truth. <BR> <BR>I gotta go before my MS flares up and I can&#39;t move in the morning.  <BR> <BR>Steve <BR> <BR>&#40;ps, Victor - I am just glad you aren&#39;t along when I go to see the in-laws. That would be the last place I&#39;d need my id spoken aloud.&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
