<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11138"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Yomama<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Yomama<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->thank you so much for letting me know about when his printer broke down at home he started using the one at his church... ok folks there you have it ...!!!this may sound very stupid and very elementry,  but if he had a printer that broke down that tells me that he had a computer at home too.  wow, now lets look at this elementary and dumb as it may seem, it seems at least to me that mr rader was at least following this and other boards about himself...after all somewhere he said...&#34;how many do i have to kill til i get on the news&#34; or something to that effect...he wanted publicity and lots of it !!! this board was a very good way for him to feed his ego and such but at the same time it made him more paranoid if for no other reason that people started saying that they live right there in the area where he was living and killing...most of the time serial killers are ahead because they are the only one that knows what they have done and what they are doing and what they will do...that gives them the advantage...but this time btk had to not only come on this and other boards  about himself to see what other people were thinking and doing.  yes, because of his ego but also because he was getting worried because he had to see if anybody was really on to him...some of you lived very close to him and this made him paranoid...not a good thing for a serial killer to deal with.  but at any rate,  i feel that this board really helped mr rader to feel uncomfortable which is not good for a serial killer either..i would say that some of you were getting way to close for his comfort zone and i sure hope that tom comes up with some other maniac for us to terrorize.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11138-->
<!--Post: 11139--><!--Time: 1110465892-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11139"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Yomama<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Yomama<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->embersage, don&#39;t pay no attention to any negative comments about your posts or anything else.  i wasn&#39;t getting any news about btk where i live and i found this board and it really helped me to stay informed about what was going on with the case and different theorys.  i live one state over from kansas and was worried as you can well imagine so i thank you and everybody that posted.  i&#39;m so glad that you were here !!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11139-->
<!--Post: 11146--><!--Time: 1110476574-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11146"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lctrip<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lctrip<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 9:42 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember - everyone of course is entitled to their opinion, Woolpainter included.  That doesn&#39;t mean he/she is right.  I&#39;m sure some folks here feel you post too much, others see it as appropriate, a few maybe not enough, and there are probably a bunch who don&#39;t care. <BR> <BR>If you let this person drive you off the board, you let them win.  You have put far too much of your time and effort into this to let that happen.  Your thoughts and input are of interest to many of us.  Do not let one individual bully you into thinking you are not adding value. <BR> <BR>I applaud your honesty in doing what Woolpainter asked you to do in spite of the fact that it was less than complimentary towards you. <BR> <BR>Woolpainter, heres a thought for you.  If you are so bothered by us EPS posters then stay off the board!  Out of site, out of mind, problem solved. <BR> <BR>Johno, thanks for the laugh.  Pity we as a group are spread out all over the country, otherwise we could set up some 12 step meetings to battle EPS.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
