<!--Post: 11156--><!--Time: 1110482972-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11156"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 11:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think bluepup and nancydrew are gone but just in case they aren&#39;t, this is for them. What did either of you ever bring to the table? Neither of you have any proof that this board and all the others did not have any effect on his actions. Of course LE would love to think that, but then again, WHEN did they first get possession of a BTK missive. And what did they do with it?  <BR>Any of us who read E&#39;s posts and also study cold cases, know full well that there are so many dots out there to connect in re other possible serials that it is beyond any small group&#39;s abilities. Just the amount of unsolveds in Kansas shocks me, think how many more there are out here in Calif. Le needs all the help it can get, and remember we do not operate under budget constraints, and do not have the burden of current cases demanding our attention. Plus we need not concern ourselves with jurisdictional issues, should read turf wars. <BR>If LE wishes to take the credit, so be it, we will know what we have accomplished. <BR>I also listened to Dr. Morrison last night, interesting, but strictly a gloss over. She is so stupid that she couldn&#39;t even remember Juan Corona&#39;s name. Also she said that there are no female serials. Funny, I go past &#34;Dirty Dorthea&#34;s house just about every day. Also she stated that her definition of a serial is at least seven victims, unknown to the perp. New one on me. I&#39;ll be back in a few days, gotta go over to EAR-ONS. She also stated that there is no such thing as a serial rapist transforming into a serial killer. Oops, after 27 or so years it looks like we need a whole new theory on that one. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
