</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 12:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you everyone for the support and Night Driver, I agree while trying to locate the Identity of the 1986 female vic in Saline we are coming across thousands of unsolved cases, The LE in Saline have been wonderful in helping us and everyone on this broad is contributing This for me is what it&#39;s all about, People working together for the common good. I could care less who get&#39;s the credit, when the families start to get the closure they deserve, my reward is and will be knowing they are no longer wondering what happened. Could you imagine how painful it must be to Kiss your loved one goodbye, Once they walk out the door to go to work or school and never see them again, try living with that every single day of your life, then ask me why we are still here.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
