<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11169"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 1:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Just stopped by because of an amazing discovery!!!! <BR>The Christmas lights on Rader&#39;s house &#40;once I zoomed, enhanced, used photo shop, inverted, and re-aligned&#41; seem to be in a pattern!!! <BR>red red green green red red green greed red green. <BR>It must be a clue!!  He&#39;s sending a message!  I think red represents what his wife knew, and green is a hint to where the next drop would have been. <BR> <BR>Come on, lighten up, you guys!  Don&#39;t take yourselves so seriously.   <BR> <BR>By the way, I  enjoyed reading your assumptions about me &#40;new hip, etc&#41;.  They&#39;re about as accurate as your theories on BTK were. <BR> <BR>Okay, really, I&#39;ll try to be quiet now.  Good Luck, Magical Thinkers!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
