<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11244"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 11:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sorry Nancy, too much has happened to me lately, and too much is happening around me to lighten up right now. I am a recent victim of identity theft and what does our new AG want? He wants to crack down on obscenity. If we don&#39;t get serious, who will? After walking the walk at the Maggiore crime scene last month, I got a lot more serious. Try it some time. As Senior Crown said over on the A&amp;E Board, &#34;Where do we stand? We stand with the victims.&#34;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
