<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11247"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 11:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Why were you looking at Denny&#39;s house. Denny doesn&#39;t live there anymore. No one is home. The case is wrapped up. Nothing more to see here folks, now, let&#39;s move along.It&#39;s all over. No point in hanging on. It&#39;ll all come out in the trial. The neighbors in the photo deserve their privacy, so let&#39;s quit staring at the images. It&#39;s just another house. Don&#39;t make an ass of yourself by looking at it.The police will take care of it. Just leave it to the professionals, they obviously know what their doing...the ones in the picture I mean. So don&#39;t make a big thing out of the Christmas lights, cause there is nothing ironic about them being there. No one takes their lights down until July. This is America for god sake, so trust in your officials and quit asking questions because it&#39;s not patriotic. Think what would happen if everyone started suspecting the government officials of having some &#34;private agenda&#34; for God&#39;s sake. The country would lapse into total chaos. People with authority are chosen for their honesty and goodwill toward all people and we should let them do their job and quit interfereing by asking questions and such. For Christ sake if god would have wanted us to know what was going on around us we would have been born with ESP!!!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
