<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11286"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Freya<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Freya<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 7:58 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bluepup, thanks for starting this thread. Though I don&#39;t agree will all of your opening points, I think your reason for creating this thread is valid and it&#39;s always important to remember that all opinions are valid even the ones we don&#39;t like. This of course applies to everyone, though some here tend to forget that. That&#39;s ok, too.  <BR> <BR>One thing that has amazed me since I started posting on CatchBTk is the tendency among some posters to debate back and forth over whether the site has helped to catch Dennis Rader, and--for what it&#39;s worth--my answer is, &#34;Who cares?&#34; If this site had helped in the investigation in any way, or influenced Rader to &#34;trip up&#34;, that&#39;s fabulous, but let&#39;s not forget that the one success of this website that is not debateable <BR>&#40;considering the number of &#34;hits&#34;&#41; is that it increased awareness of the BTK crimes and informed the public. Why can&#39;t this be a good enough result? If not for this site, I never would have learned about what incredible people his victims were, and how strong their surviving families members continue to be today. I&#39;ve also met some really great people here. <BR> <BR>So Bluepup, you are free to voice your criticism, but a few &#34;obsessed&#34; posters don&#39;t prevent me &#40;can&#39;t speak for everyone else&#41; from getting loads of information that I would have had to search for otherwise. If some people believe that their posts are aiding law enforcement, who does that hurt? If you trusted WPD, etc. to conduct a thorough investigation then logically you should trust them not to be impeded by the theories of individual citizens.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
