<!--Post: 11300--><!--Time: 1110563107-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11300"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nightdriver<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nightdriver<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 9:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, you seem to have a big problem. It&#39;s called reading comprehension. First, the scene I mentioned was that of another case in a completely different state. It&#39;s a double murder, unsolved for 27 years. One other point: You say this is all wrapped up? Go stick your head in the sand somewhere. That way you won&#39;t see all the crap going on around you. The rest of your post sounds to me like you are writing that from the perspective of someone who has something to hide. It&#39;s generally so myopic as to be laughable. Talk about making an ass of one&#39;s self. <BR>Freya: Very well said except for one thing. &#34;Who cares?&#34; Since both the Internet and serial offenders seem to be with us for the forseeable future, it would seem to me to be valuable information as to how any of us may have influenced his actions. Also if indeed he did make posts, which ones they were, and how close were we to identifying the real ones as opposed to the pretenders. It is a fact that people of this nature want to be recognized for their &#34;feats&#34;. If we know what works and what doesn&#39;t, we&#39;ll all be sitting around waiting for the next serial offender, knowing full well how to give him all the recognition he deserves. When I first saw Denny&#39;s mug shot, I didn&#39;t stop laughing for a minute. That expression on his face was so hilarious, I couldn&#39;t believe it. I can&#39;t wait to see the mug shot of the next serial that gets nailed. With the help of some of us, hopefully.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
